msgid "EMStudio commands"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Generated from EMStudio 85f69cd for em API 1.2.0.*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Every command of EMStudio's menus (41 rows of the command table, 41 reachable from Python), the items the operating system draws in the macOS menu bar, and the keys and gestures of the key map. ``em.app.commands.run(command_id, **slots)`` reaches a command by the id in the first column."
msgstr ""

msgid "How ``run_command`` reaches the page"
msgstr ""

msgid "``src/s3dgraphy/em/__init__.py:233`` — em.app.commands.run -\\> host app run\\_command"
msgstr ""

msgid "``src/s3dgraphy/em/host.py:147`` — NullHost: NotAvailable outside a host"
msgstr ""

msgid "``tools/em_py.py:576`` — EMStudioApp.run\\_command asks the page: request kind \"command\" with id and slots"
msgstr ""

msgid "``frontend/src/py-session.ts:364`` — PySession answers the request through the page's host.command(id, slots); false -\\> error py.noCommand"
msgstr ""

msgid "``frontend/src/main.ts:65807`` — the page's host hook: command -\\> runCommand(id)"
msgstr ""

msgid "``frontend/src/menu-ui.ts:182`` — runCommand: plugin:\\<id\\>/\\<cmd\\> -\\> plugin invocation; otherwise findRow(id) and click the row's button"
msgstr ""

msgid "``frontend/src/menu-ui.ts:201`` — findRow: only rows of kind \"cmd\" in MENUS (sub-menus walked)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Plugin commands are reachable too, as ``plugin:<plugin>/<command>`` (registered at run time, not listed here; see ``em.plugins``). Slots are accepted by the API but not forwarded to the command by the page. No command declares whether it writes to the graph: the column says ``unknown``."
msgstr ""

